          up: {"title":"Appropriate or inappropriate online? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Some of these actions seem harmless, and some are done with good intentions. Judge each by the rules of conduct.</p>","items":[{"t":"Using Reply All only when every person on the thread needs the information.","bin":0,"fb":"Checking recipients is part of thinking before sending."},{"t":"Posting a news story on the class page with the headline only, and no link or source.","bin":1,"fb":"Sharing someone else's content without citing the source breaks the rule to cite sources."},{"t":"Muting a heated group chat and replying calmly the next morning.","bin":0,"fb":"Waiting until you are calm is thinking before sending."},{"t":"\"Liking\" a meme that mocks a classmate, without commenting.","bin":1,"fb":"A like spreads and rewards the mockery, which makes the bystander part of the repetition."},{"t":"Asking a friend before posting a group photo in which she appears.","bin":0,"fb":"Asking first avoids unauthorised sharing of her image."},{"t":"Screenshotting a bully's messages and posting them publicly to shame him.","bin":1,"fb":"Good intentions, but it spreads the victim's private content further. Keep evidence privately and report it."},{"t":"Disagreeing in a forum: \"I see it differently, and here is a source that supports my view.\"","bin":0,"fb":"Respectful disagreement about ideas, with a cited source."},{"t":"Writing an anonymous review of a restaurant that includes false claims, to hurt its business.","bin":1,"fb":"Deliberately false, harmful comments are inflammatory and dishonest, even when anonymous."},{"t":"Sending a private message to a classmate to check she is all right after an unkind post.","bin":0,"fb":"Respectful, caring and private: good online behaviour."}],"win":"Sound judgement. The hardest cards were the \"like\", the public screenshot and the uncredited headline: each seems small or well meant, but each breaks a rule of conduct."}
